# What the `genlayer` job in .github/workflows/gates.yml asks for, before resolution.
#
# The job installs the COMPILED sibling, `ci-genlayer.txt`, which names this set plus everything it
# drags in, each with its hashes. This file is the intent; that one is what runs.
#
# THIS SET NEEDS PYTHON >= 3.12, UNLIKE ITS THREE SIBLINGS. `genlayer-py` and `genlayer-test`
# declare `requires_python: ">=3.12"` - this repository's own interpreter is 3.10
# (GL-harness-notes.md, D-63). `pip-compile`, which compiled the other three `.in` files, runs under
# THIS repository's 3.10 and cannot resolve this set at all. Regenerate this one file from a real
# Python 3.12:
#
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python 3.12 --prerelease allow -c /tmp/gl-constraints.txt \
#       -o requirements/ci-genlayer.txt requirements/ci-genlayer.in
#
# where /tmp/gl-constraints.txt (not committed) holds the three lines `iniconfig==2.3.0`,
# `pluggy==1.6.0`, `pytest==9.1.1`: the versions `ci-tests.txt` and `ci-shipped.txt` pin, so that
# `tests/test_pip_pinned.py` (one version of a package across the sets) stays green. The
# unconstrained resolution picks newer ones; `genlayer-test` runs on the pinned pytest.
#
# T-GLR-04: the set moved to the toolchain that matches the GenVM runner Bradbury Phase 2 executes
# (py-genlayer `babwp9t37j...`, header `# v0.3.0`): `genlayer-test` 0.30.0rc2 is the direct harness
# that loads that runner's `.zip` form, `genvm-linter` 0.11.1rc2 the first linter that can load it,
# and both are published to PyPI only as release candidates (hence `--prerelease allow`; one
# transitive dependency, `py-ecc`, is a beta too). The old `genlayer-py<0.17.0` metadata conflict
# (GL-harness-notes.md SS7a) is gone, so no `--override` file is needed any more; the install keeps
# `--no-deps` anyway, because the compiled file already names the full closure with hashes.
genlayer-py==0.19.0rc2
genlayer-test==0.30.0rc2
genvm-linter==0.11.1rc2
